# --- Node (the React client) ---
node_modules/
dist/

# The client's build output, and therefore not source. Vite's outDir points
# straight here (see vite.config.ts), so every `npm run build` rewrites the
# whole folder with freshly hashed filenames -- committed, that is a diff of
# renamed binaries on every build. The folder itself is gone from git too: it
# no longer holds a .gitkeep, because emptyOutDir deletes everything it finds
# except .git. A fresh clone therefore has no wwwroot until the client is
# built, which is correct -- the application has nothing to serve until then,
# and it answers 404 and says so.
src/LandMoney.Web/wwwroot/

# --- The migration bundle -- #37 ---
#
# Build output, and it is 128 MB of it. It is produced by ci.yml from every
# commit and downloaded as an artifact when deploying, so a copy sitting here is
# a working file rather than a thing to keep -- and one committed by accident
# would be a binary in the history for ever.
efbundle
efbundle.exe

